{"count":1095,"next":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=6&page_size=100","previous":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=4&page_size=100","results":[{"id":606,"title":"AFP Commander-in-Chief lauds outstanding units for dismantling Guerilla Fronts","slug":"afp-commander-in-chief-lauds-outstanding-units-for-dismantling-guerilla-fronts","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Commander-in-Chief, Armed Forces of the Philippines, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr, led the awarding of the Campaign Streamer awards to outstanding military units during the Year-End 2023 Command Conference conducted on January 15 at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/ban.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Commander-in-Chief, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr., attaches the campaign streamers awarded to the 801Bde, 8ID, PA, received by BGen Lenart R Lelina PA, during the Command Conference conducted on January 15, 2024, in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.  (Photo by Mr Fred Abuda Jr, DND)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-15T08:43:44+08:00","hits":1626},{"id":607,"title":"AFP conducts command conference with President Marcos Jr","slug":"afp-conducts-command-conference-with-president-marcos-jr","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines held its yearend Command Conference on January 15 with the Commander in Chief, President Ferdinand Marcos Jr, in attendance to hear updates on the AFP’s campaigns and programs and deliver his guidance.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the AFP, led top military officers from the General Headquarters, AFP-wide Support and Separate Units, Major Services, and Unified Commands, and commanders of the army, air force, and naval units on the ground.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/CC3.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr leads the AFP Command Conference on January 15 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. He was joined by the Executive Secretary Lucas Bersamin, Special Assistant to the President Antonio Lagdameo Jr, Secretary of National Defense Gilbert Teodoro Jr, and AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-15T08:41:20+08:00","hits":2296},{"id":608,"title":"Gen. Brawner graces Ihudyat Concert 2024","slug":"gen-brawner-graces-ihudyat-concert-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA served as the Guest of Honor and Speaker during the Ihudyat Concert 2024 on January 13 conducted at the AFP Commissioned Officers Country. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his message, Gen. Brawner emphasized the rich history, traditions and impact of the University of the Philippines (UP) Reserve Officers' Training Corps (ROTC) and its contributions to serving the country. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/IC1.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA,  delivers his message during the Ihudyat 2024 on January 13, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-15T08:39:14+08:00","hits":1227},{"id":609,"title":"CSAFP dons ranks to 8 newly promoted military officers","slug":"csafp-dons-ranks-to-8-newly-promoted-military-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo Brawner Jr, donned higher ranks to eight newly promoted military officers in a ceremony held on January 12 at the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/don1.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, dons new ranks on MGen Edmundo G Peralta during the donning of ranks ceremony for newly promoted officers on January 12 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-12T16:15:14+08:00","hits":3824},{"id":610,"title":"AFP conducts 1st GFPS EXECOM meeting in 2024","slug":"afp-conducts-1st-gfps-execom-meeting-in-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines’ Gender and Development (GAD) Focal Point System (AFPGFPS) Executive Committee (EXECOM) held its first meeting in 2024 on January 11 at the AFP General Headquarters here. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/exe1.jpg","image_caption":"The AFP Vice Chief of Staff, LtGen Arthur Cordura, presides over the Gender and Development Focal Point System Executive Committee Meeting on January 11 at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-12T08:42:59+08:00","hits":754},{"id":611,"title":"DND, AFP hold Joint New Year’s Call","slug":"dnd-afp-hold-joint-new-year-s-call","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Department of National Defense and the Armed Forces of the Philippines held their traditional New Year’s Call led by Defense Secretary Gilbert Teodoro Jr and AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr on January 12 here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/nc7.jpg","image_caption":"Secretary of National Defense Gilbert Teodoro Jr welcomes General Romeo Brawner, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, to the Joint Department of National Defense-Armed Forces of the Philippines New Year's Call on January 12 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-12T08:41:15+08:00","hits":869},{"id":612,"title":"Mensahe ni General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines, sa pagdiriwang ng pista ng Itim na Nazareno sa ika-9 ng Enero 2024.","slug":"mensahe-ni-general-romeo-brawner-jr-chief-of-staff-armed-forces-of-the-philippines-sa-pagdiriwang-ng-pista-ng-itim-na-nazareno-sa-ika-9-ng-enero-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/naz%201.jpg","image_caption":"Mensahe ni General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines, sa pagdiriwang ng pista ng Itim na Nazareno sa ika-9 ng Enero 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-08T14:41:55+08:00","hits":431},{"id":613,"title":"AFP Statement on the emerging challenges of 2024","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-emerging-challenges-of-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/emec%201.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Statement on the emerging challenges of 2024","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-04T21:40:22+08:00","hits":416},{"id":614,"title":"PH, US forces successfully conduct joint training under Maritime Cooperative Activity","slug":"ph-us-forces-successfully-conduct-joint-training-under-maritime-cooperative-activity","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the United States Indo-Pacific Command (USINDOPACOM) successfully completed the second Maritime Cooperative Activity (MCA) on January 3-4, 2024.</span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The second and final day of the joint maritime exercise was marked by the performance of cross-deck maneuvers or personnel transfers, demonstrating the competencies and effectiveness of both naval forces. It also emphasized the ability of the AFP and USINDOPACOM to work seamlessly together, highlighting their expertise and readiness. The exercise also conducted a thorough communications check before concluding the activity.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/2nd%20mca.jpg","image_caption":"A Filipino pilot executes a final check of the Philippine Navy AW109 helicopter on deck USS Carl Vinson.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-04T18:38:10+08:00","hits":531},{"id":615,"title":"AFP, USINDOPACOM holds 2nd maritime cooperative activity in WPS","slug":"afp-usindopacom-holds-2nd-maritime-cooperative-activity-in-wps","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the United States Indo-Pacific Command (USINDOPACOM) commence the second iteration of the maritime cooperative activity in the West Philippine Sea from January 3 to 4, 2024.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The 2-day bilateral event will conduct passing exercises, communication checks, cross-deck exercises, joint patrols, Officer of the Watch (OW) maneuvers, and fixed-wing flight operations.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/mca%201.jpg","image_caption":"PH vessels in column formation in the vicinity of North West of Cabra, Lubang, Occidental Mindoro during the 2nd PH-US MCA on January 3, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-03T14:34:48+08:00","hits":505},{"id":616,"title":"AFP Statement on the Tsunami Warning after the 7.6 magnitude earthquake  hitting Japan on  January 1, 2024","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-tsunami-warning-after-the-7-6-magnitude-earthquake-hitting-japan-on-january-1-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/tsu.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-01T14:30:27+08:00","hits":278},{"id":617,"title":"On the anniversary of the martyrdom of our national hero, Dr. Jose P. Rizal","slug":"on-the-anniversary-of-the-martyrdom-of-our-national-hero-dr-jose-p-rizal","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/GCgug59bEAAEmjI.jpg","image_caption":"The message of General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, on the anniversary of the martyrdom of our national hero, Dr. Jose P. Rizal.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-29T14:21:21+08:00","hits":282},{"id":618,"title":"Christmas Day message of General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines.","slug":"christmas-day-message-of-general-romeo-brawner-jr-chief-of-staff-of-the-armed-forces-of-the-philippines","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/XMAS%20MESSAGE.jpg","image_caption":"Christmas Day message of General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-24T14:18:32+08:00","hits":180},{"id":619,"title":"AFP HONORS OUTSTANDING PEACE PARTNERS","slug":"afp-honors-outstanding-peace-partners","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines, in celebration of its 88th anniversary, recognized individuals, groups, and people’s organizations for their invaluable support to the military’s “Pagkakaisa” campaign in a ceremony on December 21 at the General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/viber_image_2023-12-21_12-36-37-137%201.jpg","image_caption":"Mr Verlin Ruiz, former president of the Defense Press Corps, receives the Pagkakaisa Award from the Chief of Staff AFP, General Romeo Brawner Jr, during the awarding ceremony at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on December 21.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-21T14:09:47+08:00","hits":293},{"id":620,"title":"AFP Chief visits remote base in mountainous Samar town","slug":"afp-chief-visits-remote-base-in-mountainous-samar-town","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, continued his visit of the military's remotest stations and personally delivered Christmas gifts and wishes to the forward operating detachment in Las Navas, Samar and the 8th Infantry Division on December 20.</span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">In his stopover at the 8th Infantry Division headquarters in Catbalogan City, General Brawner Jr also lauded the unit to complete the end of the communist armed conflict in the area.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/411675882_732749758887437_5700475064878115232_n.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, talks to the troops of the 8th Infantry Division assigned at the forward operating detachment in Las Navas, Samar on December 20.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-20T17:05:00+08:00","hits":314},{"id":621,"title":"CSAFP HONORS FALLEN SOLDIERS IN A WREATH-LAYING CEREMONY","slug":"csafp-honors-fallen-soldiers-in-a-wreath-laying-ceremony","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – As part of the celebration of the 88th Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Anniversary, The Chief of Staff, AFP (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA, paid tribute to fallen soldiers in a Wreath-laying Ceremony conducted on December 15, 2023, at the Libingan ng mga Bayani, Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The wreath-laying, aimed at commemorating military personnel who made the ultimate sacrifice in the line of duty, and held simultaneously at different camps nationwide, is one of the activities lined up to celebrate the AFP’s 88th anniversary that will culminate on December 21.<br />","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/CSAFP%20HONORS%20FALLEN%20SOLDIERS.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr. pays tribute to fallen soldiers during a Wreath-laying Ceremony conducted on December 15, 2023, at the Libingan ng mga Bayani, Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-15T13:56:31+08:00","hits":338},{"id":622,"title":"CSAFP MEETS WITH MULTI-SECTORAL ADVISORY BOARD","slug":"csafp-meets-with-multi-sectoral-advisory-board","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), sat in an introductory meeting with the AFP Multi-Sectoral Governance Council (MSGC), the military’s security sector reform partner, on December 12 at the General Headquarters here.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Composed of representatives from various sector of society, the MSGC provides expert advice and recommendations in the AFP’s policies, plans, and programs as well as to champion the AFP Transformation Roadmap and help improve transparency and accountability. It’s chaired currently by Mr Francisco Del Rosario Jr of the Institute for Solidarity in Asia.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">“On behalf of the AFP, I want to thank the MSGC. We appreciate the time and effort that you are spending and your willingness to held the AFP. In return, the AFP commits to our pursuit of good governance, transparency, and accountability,” General Brawner Jr said in his closing message.</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Photos by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/CSAFP%20MEETS%20WITH%20MSDB.jpg","image_caption":"Senior officers of the Armed Forces of the Philippines led by General Romeo Brawner Jr pose for a photo with the chairperson and members of the AFP Multi-Sectoral Governance Council during the introductory meeting on December 12 at Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-12T13:52:11+08:00","hits":390},{"id":623,"title":"GENERAL BRAWNER JOINS AYUNGIN RESUPPLY MISSION, CONVEYS PRESIDENT’S MESSAGE","slug":"general-brawner-joins-ayungin-resupply-mission-conveys-president-s-message","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -- The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr, visited BRP Sierra Madre in Ayungin Shoal on Sunday, December 10, 2023, to personally convey President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr’s appreciation and yuletide greetings to our troops stationed aboard the vessel.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">General Brawner is the first sitting AFP Chief of Staff to have set foot on the ship. During their journey, he experienced firsthand the risks faced by the regular resupply missions as the China Coast Guard and its maritime militia continue their attempts to obstruct said missions.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/GENERAL%20BRAWNER%20RESUPPLY%20MISSION.jpg","image_caption":"The AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo S Brawner Jr sharing lunch with the personnel of the BRP Sierra Madre on December 10, 2023.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-11T13:48:19+08:00","hits":272},{"id":624,"title":"Gov't forces capture MSU bombing suspect","slug":"govt-forces-capture-msu-bombing-suspect","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--Combined troops of Task Force Marawi and Marawi City police captured on December 6 a certain Jafar Gamo Sultan, a.k.a. Jaf/Kurot, who is one of the accomplices in the bombing at Mindanao State University last week.<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The suspect, who was apprehended in an operation in Brgy Dulay Proper in Marawi, is companion of a certain Omar, the person identified by witnesses to have placed the improvised explosive device at the Dimaporo Gymnasium. Also seized by troops are two motorcyles.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">This development shows the seriousness of the government in capturing the perpetrators of the terrorist attack on innocent civilians and in ensuring that similar incidents will not happen again. It also demonstrates the AFP's commitment to its mandate as protector of the people and the state.</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/SUSPECT.jpg","image_caption":"-Combined troops of Task Force Marawi and Marawi City police captured on December 6 a certain Jafar Gamo Sultan, a.k.a. Jaf/Kurot, who is one of the accomplices in the bombing at Mindanao State University.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-08T13:44:36+08:00","hits":184},{"id":625,"title":"CSAFP VISITS MILITARY PATIENTS, LEADS AFP MENTAL HEALTH PROGRAM ADVOCACY LAUNCHING","slug":"csafp-visits-military-patients-leads-afp-mental-health-program-advocacy-launching","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA, visited military patients and led the launching of the AFP Mental Health Program Advocacy on December 06 at the Victoriano Luna Medical Center (VLMC).<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The CSAFP’s visit aims to personally check on and boost the morale of patients admitted at the VLMC and to officially launch the AFP Mental Health Program Advocacy with the goal of promoting mental health awareness.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/CSAFP%20VISITS%20MILITARY%20PATIENTS.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-06T13:41:34+08:00","hits":324},{"id":626,"title":"CSAFP ORDERS TROOPS IN MARAWI CITY TO GO AFTER TERROR SUSPECTS","slug":"csafp-orders-troops-in-marawi-city-to-go-after-terror-suspects","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines seeks to wrap up operations against the Daulah Islamiyah and the perpetrators of the terrorist attack at the Mindanao State University (MSU) in Marawi City on December 3.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the AFP, led the Command Conference on December 4 with senior military officers from the General Headquarters and top commanders in the Western Mindanao Command where he relayed the orders of President Ferdinand Marcos Jr in response to the terrorist attack.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/CSAFP%20ORDERS%20TROOPS%20IN%20MARAWI.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, and top military and police commanders in Western Mindanao sit down at a press conference at the headquarters of the 103rd Infantry Brigade, Marawi City on December 4.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-04T16:39:01+08:00","hits":188},{"id":627,"title":"AFP Statement on the Marawi Explosion","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-marawi-explosion","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) strongly condemns the heinous act of terror that transpired in Mindanao State University (MSU), Marawi City, on Sunday, December 3, 2023.<br /> <br />At approximately 7:14 a.m., during the first Sunday of Advent mass attended by students and teachers, an explosion rocked the Dimaporo Gymnasium, resulting in the loss of four lives and injury of at least 50 individuals.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/AFP%20STATEMENT%20ME.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Statement on the Marawi Explosion","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-12-03T21:34:41+08:00","hits":357},{"id":628,"title":"Army Shooting Team bags medals in ASEAN Rifle Meet","slug":"army-shooting-team-bags-medals-in-asean-rifle-meet","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Philippine Army Shooting Contingent (PASCON) brought home medals from the 31st Association of South East Asian (ASEAN) Armies Rifle Meet (AARM) hosted by the Royal Thai Army on November 16-25, 2023 at the Infantry Center, Prachuap, Khiri Khan (Hua Hin), Thailand.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/ARMY%20SHOOTING%20TEAM.jpg","image_caption":"The Philippine Army Shooting Contingent (PASCON) during the 31st Association of South East Asian (ASEAN) Armies Rifle Meet (AARM) hosted by the Royal Thai Army from November 16-25, 2023 in Thailand.  (Photo from PASCON)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-27T21:00:12+08:00","hits":485},{"id":629,"title":"AFP, ADF aircraft conduct joint air patrol in WPS","slug":"afp-adf-aircraft-conduct-joint-air-patrol-in-wps","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — Pilots and crew from the </span><a class=\"x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x6umtig x1b1mbwd xaqea5y xav7gou x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x16tdsg8 x1hl2dhg xggy1nq x1a2a7pz xt0b8zv x1qq9wsj xo1l8bm\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"link\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/armedforcesofthephilippines?__cft__[0]=AZWl6L3lzh22adt8RjLxOE7MOoAM44oVL003xD9EH2EyCUbL0JGwRUlUaOapy3P3Dom0e_V089ZmS32HSTgfA6JgYOo93v033k9YIzv-r5h_-lC1qDsqx6mMTmuSxAHTSrvlFewvJny9iGYhqqcbhSTDkZweazJ4rSIZbVodaqBB2nN77inHORInqvRFc7o_dJ0&amp;__tn__=-]K-R\"><span class=\"xt0psk2\">Armed Forces of the Philippines</span></a><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"> (AFP) and the </span><a class=\"x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x6umtig x1b1mbwd xaqea5y xav7gou x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x16tdsg8 x1hl2dhg xggy1nq x1a2a7pz xt0b8zv x1qq9wsj xo1l8bm\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"link\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/Australian-Defence-Force-113801821963346/?__cft__[0]=AZWl6L3lzh22adt8RjLxOE7MOoAM44oVL003xD9EH2EyCUbL0JGwRUlUaOapy3P3Dom0e_V089ZmS32HSTgfA6JgYOo93v033k9YIzv-r5h_-lC1qDsqx6mMTmuSxAHTSrvlFewvJny9iGYhqqcbhSTDkZweazJ4rSIZbVodaqBB2nN77inHORInqvRFc7o_dJ0&amp;__tn__=kK-R\"><span class=\"xt0psk2\">Australian Defence Force</span></a><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"> (ADF) successfully performed a joint air patrol in the West Philippine Sea on November 26, 2023.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The <a class=\"x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x6umtig x1b1mbwd xaqea5y xav7gou x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x16tdsg8 x1hl2dhg xggy1nq x1a2a7pz xt0b8zv x1qq9wsj xo1l8bm\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"link\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/piopaf?__cft__[0]=AZWl6L3lzh22adt8RjLxOE7MOoAM44oVL003xD9EH2EyCUbL0JGwRUlUaOapy3P3Dom0e_V089ZmS32HSTgfA6JgYOo93v033k9YIzv-r5h_-lC1qDsqx6mMTmuSxAHTSrvlFewvJny9iGYhqqcbhSTDkZweazJ4rSIZbVodaqBB2nN77inHORInqvRFc7o_dJ0&amp;__tn__=-]K-R\"><span class=\"xt0psk2\">Philippine Air Force</span></a>'s A29B Super Tucano, N-22 Nomad, <a class=\"x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x6umtig x1b1mbwd xaqea5y xav7gou x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 xe8uvvx xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r xexx8yu x4uap5 x18d9i69 xkhd6sd x16tdsg8 x1hl2dhg xggy1nq x1a2a7pz xt0b8zv x1qq9wsj xo1l8bm\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"link\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/PhilippineNavy?__cft__[0]=AZWl6L3lzh22adt8RjLxOE7MOoAM44oVL003xD9EH2EyCUbL0JGwRUlUaOapy3P3Dom0e_V089ZmS32HSTgfA6JgYOo93v033k9YIzv-r5h_-lC1qDsqx6mMTmuSxAHTSrvlFewvJny9iGYhqqcbhSTDkZweazJ4rSIZbVodaqBB2nN77inHORInqvRFc7o_dJ0&amp;__tn__=-]K-R\"><span class=\"xt0psk2\">Philippine Navy</span></a>'s BNI2A aircraft, and Australian Defence Force's P-8 Poseidon Maritime Surveillance aircraft demonstrated cooperation and camaraderie as part of the AFP-ADF Maritime Cooperative Activity (MCA).</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The AFP-ADF MCA aims to enhance maritime interoperability and deepen the PH-AUS strategic partnership as signed by President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr and Australian Prime Minister Anthony Albanese in September.///</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photo from Western Command, AFP)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/AFP%20ADF%20IN%20WPS.jpg","image_caption":"Pilots and crew from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the Australian Defence Force (ADF) successfully performed a joint air patrol in the West Philippine Sea on November 26, 2023. ","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-26T17:26:27+08:00","hits":275},{"id":630,"title":"AFP Commander-in-Chief leads 73rd FSRR Anniversary","slug":"afp-commander-in-chief-leads-73rd-fsrr-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The First Scout Ranger Regiment, Philippine Army celebrated its 73rd Anniversary with the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Commander-in-Chief, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr on November 25 at Camp Tecson, San Miguel, Bulacan.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Also present during the event was Defense Secretary Gilberto Teodoro Jr; The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA; Philippine Army Commanding General, LtGen Roy Galido; and the Regiment Commander, BGen Isagani Criste.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/FSRR%20ANNIVERSARY.jpg","image_caption":"The AFP Commander-in-Chief, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr with the Defense Secretary Gilberto Teodoro Jr; The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA; Philippine Army Commanding General, LtGen Roy Galido; and the Regiment Commander, BGen Isagani Criste PA during the 73rd Anniversary of the First Scout Ranger Regiment, Philippine Army on November 25 in San Miguel, Bulacan.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-25T19:20:41+08:00","hits":649},{"id":631,"title":"AFP, AUS DEFENCE FORCE COMMENCE 3-DAY MARITIME COOPERATIVE ACTIVITY","slug":"afp-aus-defence-force-commence-3-day-maritime-cooperative-activity","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the Australian Defence Force (ADF) will conduct a Maritime Cooperative Activity (MCA) on November 25-27, 2023.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/AFP%20AUS%20DEFENCE%20FORCE%20COMMENCE%203-DAY%20MARITIME%20COOPERATIVE%20ACTIVITY.jpg","image_caption":"The Philippine Navy's BRP Davao Del Sur and Australian Navy's HMAS Toowoomba performed officer of the watch (OOW) Maneuvers as part of the Maritime Cooperative Activity (MCA) on November 25, 2023 in Palawan.  (Photo from Western Command, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-25T13:19:28+08:00","hits":259},{"id":632,"title":"Joint AFP-PNP-PCG ETDC conference concludes","slug":"joint-afp-pnp-pcg-etdc-conference-concludes","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Joint Armed Forces of the Philippines, Philippine National Police, and Philippine Coast Guard Education, Training, and Doctrine Cell (JAPPETDC) 4th Quarter 2023 conference was concluded on November 23 at the Daza Park Pavilion here. </p>\r\n<p>Based on consolidated reports, a total of 36 trainings on combat, search and rescue, communications, law enforcement, and other matters were held for 427 military, police, and coast guard personnel this year.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/viber_image_2023-11-24_13-16-10-644.jpg","image_caption":"Participants of the Joint Armed Forces of the Philippines, Philippine National Police, and Philippine Coast Guard Education, Training, and Doctrine Cell 4th Quarter 2023 conference pose for a photo on November 23 at Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. (Photo by SSg Amagan/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-24T05:48:09+08:00","hits":517},{"id":633,"title":"PH-US vessels conduct tactical exercise in WPS","slug":"ph-us-vessels-conduct-tactical-exercise-in-wps","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines and the US Indo-Pacific Command conducted maritime tactical exercises as part of the three-day maritime cooperative activity (MCA) in the West Philippine Sea on November 23.</p>\r\n<p>Two vessels of the Philippine Navy, the BRP Jose Rizal and BRP Gregorio Del Pilar, performed cross deck operations, officer of the watch maneuvers, and publication and communication exercises with the USS Gabrielle Giffords. The MCA is expected to conclude at 6 p.m. today with the USS Giffords breaking off west of mainland Palawan.</p>\r\n<p>The MCA is an approved activity of the Mutual Defense Board-Security Engagement Board and within the framework of the PH-US Mutual Defense Treaty. It was aimed at testing protocols and further enhancing interoperability between the AFP and USINDOPACOM.</p>\r\n<p>#AFPyoucanTRUST</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/viber_image_2023-11-23_17-14-10-663.jpg","image_caption":"BRP Jose Rizal (FF150), and USS Gabriel Giffords (LCS 10) during their tactical exercise in the West Philippine Sea on November 23 as part of the three-day maritime cooperative activity.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-24T05:37:53+08:00","hits":427},{"id":634,"title":"AFP Chief lauds Chaplain Service on its 86th Anniversary","slug":"afp-chief-lauds-chaplain-service-on-its-86th-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA joined the 86th Anniversary Celebration of the Chaplain Service, AFP (CHS AFP) on November 23 at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p>The CSAFP commended the CHS AFP for its role as the “Core and the Moral Force of Incalculable Value in Providing Qualitative Enhancement of Values in the AFP.”</p>\r\n<p>“As military officers and religious leaders, your guidance and leadership have a profound impact on the beliefs and identity of our uniformed and non-uniformed personnel. Your open-mindedness and respect for the beliefs and practices of others contribute to inclusivity and harmony, essential elements for promoting peace and development in our country,” said General Brawner Jr.///</p>\r\n<p>(Photos by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/viber_image_2023-11-23_18-01-26-990.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA, The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, delivers his inspirational remarks during the 86th Anniversary Celebration of the Chaplain Service, AFP (CHS AFP) on November 23 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-24T05:36:24+08:00","hits":934},{"id":635,"title":"CEISSAFP celebrates 25th anniversary","slug":"ceissafp-celebrates-25th-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Communications, Electronics, and Information Systems Service of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CEISSAFP), the unit charged with providing effective and secure command and control infrastructure in the military, celebrated its 25th founding anniversary on November 23. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, graced the event where he lauded CEISSAFP’s innovation and dedication in performing its vital role in the AFP’s mission. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/viber_image_2023-11-23_18-37-33-743.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, Deputy Chief of Staff AFP, leads the inauguration of the CEISSAFP Repair and Maintenance Facility during the CEISSAFP founding anniversary on November 23 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.  Photo by A2C Castro/PAOAFP","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-24T05:34:52+08:00","hits":2801},{"id":636,"title":"AFP honors UN military observers and peacekeepers, soldier-athletes","slug":"afp-honors-un-military-observers-and-peacekeepers-soldier-athletes","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA recognized the achievements of the United Nations Military Observers and Peacekeeping Force Staff Officers, 19th Asian Games Sepaktakraw Bronze Medalists, and the AFP Women’s Volleyball Team in a ceremony conducted on November 24 at the General Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Chief congratulated the awardees and encouraged them to continue fostering a competitive spirit and inspiring others to strive for greatness in their respective fields to actively contribute to the protection and security of the nation. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/viber_image_2023-11-24_10-38-12-163.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, AFP, General Romeo S Brawner Jr, and other AFP Senior Officers pose for a photo with the UN Military Observers, Peacekeeping Force Staff Officers, and soldier-athletes during a Recognition Ceremony conducted on November 24, 2023 at the General Headquarters.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-24T05:33:18+08:00","hits":394},{"id":637,"title":"BRP Yap, USS Giffords perform passing exercise in WPS","slug":"brp-yap-uss-giffords-perform-passing-exercise-in-wps","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City</strong>--The BRP Conrado Yap (PS39) and the USS Gabrielle Giffords (LCS10) performed passing exercises (PASSEX) on November 22 as part of the 3-day maritime cooperative activity (MCA).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The two ships met and linked up last night west of Lubang Island and completed the exercises aimed at testing communications capabilities for real-life  scenarios.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The MCA demonstrates the commitment of the AFP and USINDOPACOM to the PH-US alliance and in maintaining regional stability and security in accordance with international law and the rules-based international order.</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/viber_image_2023-11-22_17-09-00-358.jpg","image_caption":"The BRP Conrado Yap (PS39) and the USS Gabrielle Giffords during their passing exercise in the West Philippine Sea on November 22 as part of the 3-day maritime cooperative activity. (Photo by NFNL)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-22T13:24:53+08:00","hits":226},{"id":638,"title":"AFP, USINDOPACOM conduct joint maritime cooperative activity","slug":"afp-usindopacom-conduct-joint-maritime-cooperative-activity","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the US Indo-Pacific Command (USINDOPACOM) will conduct a maritime cooperative activity (MCA) on November 21 to 23 aimed at further enhancing interoperability and fostering regional cooperation between the long-standing allies.</p>\r\n<p>The activity will commence in the vicinity of Batanes and will end in the West Philippine Sea. It will involve three navy vessels, two FA-50PH, and one A-29B Super Tucano from the side of the AFP while the US will send in one Littoral Combat Ship (LCS) and one P8-A.</p>\r\n<p>The MCA pursues PH-US principles based on a rules-based international order. It demonstrates the AFP and USINDOPACOM’s commitment to a free and open Indo-Pacific Region.#</p>\r\n<p>#AFPyoucanTRUST</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/viber_image_2023-11-22_09-00-31-586.jpg","image_caption":"PH-US aircraft conduct their joint flight on November 21 as part of the Northern Luzon leg of the maritime cooperative activity.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-22T06:10:55+08:00","hits":692},{"id":639,"title":"AFP kicks off C4ISTAR EXPO 2023","slug":"afp-kicks-off-c4istar-expo-2023","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), through the Communications, Electronics and Information Systems Service, AFP (CEISSAFP), kicks off the Command and Control, Communications, Cybersecurity, Intelligence, Surveillance, Target Acquisition and Reconnaissance (C4ISTAR) EXPO 2023 with The Vice Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Arthur M Cordura PAF as the Guest of Honor and Speaker on November 20 at the AFP Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Anchored to the theme: “The AFP Enhancing its Digital Battlefield: Adapting to the Future of Warfare,” the 2-day activity features lectures and exhibits that serve as an opportunity to engage with experts and explore the latest trends, developments, and breakthroughs in the cyber domain. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/viber_image_2023-11-20_12-26-02-924.jpg","image_caption":"The Vice Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Arthur M Cordura PAF, inspects the products displayed during the AFP C4ISTAR EXPO 2023 on November 20, 2023 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-20T05:20:43+08:00","hits":2015},{"id":640,"title":"AFP culminates AJEX DAGITPA 2023","slug":"afp-culminates-ajex-dagitpa-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines Joint Exercises Dagat-Langit-Lupa (AJEX DAGITPA) 2023 officially closed in a ceremony conducted with the Department of National Defense Senior Undersecretary Irineo Espino as the Guest of Honor and Speaker on November 17 at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AJEX DAGITPA 07-2023 opened on November 6 and was participated by forces from the AFP’s Branches of Service. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/AJEXC2.jpg","image_caption":"Senior Undersecretary Irineo Espino and AFP Senior Officers pose for a photo during the Closing Ceremony of the AJEX DAGITPA 2023 on November 17 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-17T06:22:54+08:00","hits":1026},{"id":641,"title":"AFP culminates AJEX DAGITPA 2023","slug":"afp-culminates-ajex-dagitpa-2023","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines Joint Exercises Dagat-Langit-Lupa (AJEX DAGITPA) 2023 officially closed in a ceremony conducted with the Department of National Defense Senior Undersecretary Irineo Espino as the Guest of Honor and Speaker on November 17 at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AJEX DAGITPA 07-2023 opened on November 6 and was participated by forces from the AFP’s Branches of Service. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/AJEXC2.jpg","image_caption":"Senior Undersecretary Irineo Espino and AFP Senior Officers pose for a photo during the Closing Ceremony of the AJEX DAGITPA 2023 on November 17 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-17T06:19:30+08:00","hits":893},{"id":642,"title":"AFP holds Technical and Admin Services Solidarity Fun Run","slug":"afp-holds-technical-and-admin-services-solidarity-fun-run","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Office of the Adjutant General (OTAG), Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) conducted the Technical and Administrative Services (TAS) Solidarity Fun Run with The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M) as the Guest of Honor and Speaker on November 16 at the Lapulapu Grandstand. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">With the theme: “Stride Together, Unite Forever: Stronger TAS for the AFP,” officers, enlisted personnel, Civilian Human Resources, and dependents from the TAS Corps/Service, General Headquarters, Unified Commands, AFP-Wide Support and Separate Units, and Major Services participated in the activity.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/FRUN.jpg","image_caption":"Winners and finishers were awarded during the Technical and Administrative Services (TAS) Solidarity Fun Run on November 16 at the Lapulapu Grandstand.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-16T15:51:42+08:00","hits":913},{"id":643,"title":"AFP conducts GAD Executive Briefing 2023","slug":"afp-conducts-gad-executive-briefing-2023","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines, through the Gender and Development Office, conducted a hybrid Executive Briefing to engage members of the AFP GAD Focal Point System (GFPS) on the AFP’s mainstreaming initiatives on November 15 here at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The GAD Executive Briefing was participated by the AFP and Major Services GFPS and the Chairpersons of the GAD Focal Point Committee (GFPC) from GHQ units and offices, Unified Commands, and AFP-Wide Support and Separate Units, with resource speakers from the Philippine Commission on Women (PCW) and the Office of the Presidential Adviser on Peace, Reconciliation and Unity (OPAPRU) who discussed gender mainstreaming and strategies in the defense and security sector, and the Philippine National Action Plan on Women, Peace, and Security. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/GADS.jpg","image_caption":"The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M) presents the Plaque of Appreciation to Ms. Susana Marcaida, Executive Director, Office for Local Conflict Transformation and Peace Sustainability, Office of the Presidential Adviser on Peace, Reconciliation and Unity (OPAPRU) during the AFP Gender and Development Executive Briefing 2023 on November 15 in Camp Aguinaldo.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-15T15:49:26+08:00","hits":620},{"id":644,"title":"PH, US troops open jungle obstacle course","slug":"ph-us-troops-open-jungle-obstacle-course","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--Filipino and American marines involved in this year's Kamandag Exercises built a jungle obstacle course in Camp Bojeador, Ilocos Norte on November 15.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The groundbreaking was held at the headquarters of the 4th Marine Brigade with General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, gracing the event and emphasizing its significance in strengthening the bond between the Philippines and the US.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/JOC2.jpg","image_caption":"A Philippine Marine Corps personnel tests the jungle obstacle course opened in Camp Bojeador in Ilocos Norte on November 15.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-15T07:39:04+08:00","hits":464},{"id":645,"title":"AFP tests firepower in AJEX DAGITPA","slug":"afp-tests-firepower-in-ajex-dagitpa","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) tested its combined arms firepower in a live fire exercise on November 15 as part of the AFP Joint Exercise Dagat-Langit-Lupa (AJEX DAGITPA) in Burgos, Ilocos Norte.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/AJEX3.jpg","image_caption":"Philippine Marine Corps personnel prepares artillery rounds during the combined arms live fire exercise on November 15 in Burgos, Ilocos Norte as part of the AFP Joint Exercise DAGITPA.  Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-15T04:59:29+08:00","hits":598},{"id":646,"title":"ARRIVAL HONORS | LtGen Steve Crespillo, The Inspector General AFP","slug":"arrival-honors-ltgen-steve-crespillo-the-inspector-general-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines renders arrival honors to the newly promoted LtGen Steve Crespillo, The Inspector General AFP, following the donning of ranks ceremony held at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on November 14.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The personal honors are being rendered to military officers, including the newly promoted generals and flag officers in the General Headquarters, their respective Major Service, and their own headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAOAFP</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/AH1.jpg","image_caption":"Troops of the Armed Forces of the Philippines led by the Deputy Chief of Staff for Intelligence, J2, MGen Ferdinand Barandon, renders arrival honors to the newly promoted LtGen Steve Crespillo, The Inspector General AFP, following the donning of ranks ceremony held at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on November 14.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-14T08:05:44+08:00","hits":1228},{"id":647,"title":"Six senior officers don new ranks","slug":"six-senior-officers-don-new-ranks","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Six senior military officers of the Armed Forces of the Philippines were promoted to their next higher ranks in a donning ceremony presided by General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, on November 14 at the AFP General Headquarters here. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The promoted officers were LtGen Steve Crespillo, The Inspector General AFP; MGen Arvin Lagamon, Deputy Chief of Staff for Civil-Military Operations, J7; Commodore Peter Jempsun De Guzman, Assistant Deputy Chief of Staff for Operations, AJ3; BGen Benedict Balaba, Deputy Chief of the Intelligence Service AFP; BGen Ramon Flores, Commandant of Cadets of the Philippine Military Academy; and BGen Ivan Papera, Chief of the AFP Systems Engineering Office.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/SEN2.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Steve Crespillo, The Inspector General AFP, is donned new ranks by General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the AFP. They were assisted by the former’s daughter, Sean Coleen Crespillo, during the donning of ranks ceremony on November 14 at the AFP General Headquarters in Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-14T08:03:54+08:00","hits":1033},{"id":648,"title":"CSAFP joins AJEX’ command post exercise","slug":"csafp-joins-ajex-command-post-exercise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, visited the site of the Command Post Exercise of the 2023 AFP Joint Exercise Dagat, Langit, Lupa (AJEX DAGITPA) on November 13 here.<br /> <br />The CPX aims to train designated officers and enhance their understanding of the Joint Operations Process and Procedures, and further improve their capabilities and competencies in developing joint planning and execution and grasp of unit capabilities.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/AJEXGHQ.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, is being briefed by MGen Marvin Licudine, the AJEX DAGITPA Exercise Director, during the former’s visit to the Command Post Exercise on November 13 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-13T06:19:55+08:00","hits":472},{"id":649,"title":"AFP boosts maritime security readiness in Field Training Exercise","slug":"afp-boosts-maritime-security-readiness-in-field-training-exercise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines through BRP Ramon Alcaraz (PS16), BRP Nestor Reinoso (PC380), NV320 Islander aircraft of the Philippine Navy (PN), and in collaboration with BRP Malapascua (MRRV-4403) of the Philippine Coast Guard successfully carried out Field Training Exercise on November 11, 2023 in Ilocos Norte to develop maritime cooperation and preparedness.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As part of the ongoing AFP Joint Exercises 'Dagat-Langit-Lupa' (AJEX DAGITPA), the activity demonstrated seamless collaboration between the Philippine Navy and the Philippine Coast Guard while showcasing the capabilities of military and coast guard assets. It also featured the active participation of the Special Operations Group from the PN and PCG Command in the Northern Luzon Command (NOLCOM) area of responsibility.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/FTX.jpg","image_caption":"Joint Visit, Board, Search and Seizure between NAVSOCOM and SOG PCG being carried out during the Field Training Exercise of AJEX DAGITPA.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-11T12:56:19+08:00","hits":650},{"id":650,"title":"AFP continues to gain ground against lawless elements","slug":"afp-continues-to-gain-ground-against-lawless-elements","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) continues to gain ground as sustained military operations  neutralized members of Communist Terrorist Groups (CTGs) and Local Terrorist Groups (LTGs) across the country as of October this year. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/CTG3.jpg","image_caption":"An NPA member yields to Lt. Col. Eduard Sia-ed, Commanding Officer of the 5th Infantry Battalion in Wao, Lanao del Sur on October 8. (Photo by Western Mindanao Command)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-10T06:23:17+08:00","hits":589},{"id":651,"title":"AFP welcomes French military officer","slug":"afp-welcomes-french-military-officer","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcomed BGen Caroline Salahun, Director for Asia Pacific, Armament Directorate of France Ministry of Defense, during her courtesy visit on November 10 at the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/FMO2.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Rey Alemania, Deputy Chief of Staff for Logistics, J4, receives a souvenir from BGen Caroline Salahun, Director for Asia Pacific, Armament Directorate of France Ministry of Defense during her courtesy visit on November 10 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-10T06:22:06+08:00","hits":664},{"id":652,"title":"AFP, UNOCHA hold dialogue on cooperation","slug":"afp-unocha-hold-dialogue-on-cooperation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City-- The Armed Forces of the Philippines and the United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs sat down in a dialogue on November 9 here as part of efforts to further strengthen coordination between the military and UN agencies and local and international non-government organizations in the country.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The meeting was led by BGen Arvin Lagamon, Deputy Chief of Staff for Civil Military Operations, J7, and Manja Vidic, Head of OCHA Philippines. It featured presentations on protection principles and mainstreaming and UN OCHA's Anticipatory Action and Enhancing Resilient Communities Flagship Initiative.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/UNO2.jpg","image_caption":"BGen Arvin Lagamon, Deputy Chief of Staff for Civil Military Operations, J7, welcomes Manja Vidic, Head of OCHA Philippines, on November 9 for their quarterly dialogue in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-09T09:24:55+08:00","hits":412},{"id":653,"title":"AFP hosts Closing Ceremony of PH Uniformed Services Olympics 2023","slug":"afp-hosts-closing-ceremony-of-ph-uniformed-services-olympics-2023","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines, through the Office of the Chief, Special Service, AFP, formally closed the 2023 AFP-PNP-PCG-BFP-BJMP-BuCor Olympics with Commissioner Olivia “Bong” G. Coo of the Philippine Sports Commission (PSC) as the Guest of Honor and Speaker during a ceremony conducted on November 9 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Athletes from the Philippine Army, Philippine Air Force, Philippine Navy, Philippine National Police (PNP), Philippine Coast Guard (PCG), Bureau of Fire Protection (BFP), and Bureau of Jail Management and Penology (BJMP) attended this year’s Olympics with the Philippine Army being hailed as the overall champion. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/OLY4.jpg","image_caption":"The Heads of Delegation receive their trophies for the 2023 AFP-PNP-PCG-BFP-BJMP-BuCor Olympics Closing Ceremony on November 9 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand, Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-09T09:20:53+08:00","hits":695},{"id":654,"title":"AFP Vice Chief encourages troops to be GAD champions","slug":"afp-vice-chief-encourages-troops-to-be-gad-champions","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Vice Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (VCSAFP), LtGen Arthur M Cordura PAF commended the AFP Gender and Development Office (AFPGADO) for its milestones during the celebration of its 1st Founding Anniversary Celebration on November 9 at the General Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">During his keynote speech, LtGen Cordura expressed the AFP’s support of the AFPGADO’s advocacies and initiatives under the leadership of its first-ever Chief, Col Arlene Fragé PA. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/GADB1.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Arthur M Cordura PAF, Vice Chief of Staff, AFP and Col. Arlene Fragé, Chief, AFP Gender and Development Office lead the launching of the Post-Conference CY 2023 Evaluation Handbook during the AFPGADO’s 1st Founding Anniversary Celebration on November 9 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-09T05:16:19+08:00","hits":483},{"id":655,"title":"AFP GAD Office celebrates 1st Anniversary","slug":"afp-gad-office-celebrates-1st-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — A year since its creation, the Armed Forces of the Philippines Gender and Development Office (AFPGADO) celebrates its 1st Founding Anniversary on November 8 at the General Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As part of the celebration, lecturers from the Women and Children Protection Center (WCPC) of the Philippine National Police (PNP) were invited to share best practices and raise awareness during the conduct of a Seminar on Sexual and Gender-Based Violence (SGBV) and PNP Best Practices on Treatment of SGBV Victims.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/GAD1.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Gender and Development Office Chief, Col Arlene Frage PA presents the Certificate of Appreciation to the resource speaker, PEMS Marsha T Agustin PNP during the conduct of the Seminar on Sexual and Gender-based Violence and PNP Best Practices on Treatment of SGBV Victims in celebration of the AFPGADO’s 1st Founding Anniversary on November 8 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-08T06:34:38+08:00","hits":614},{"id":656,"title":"CSAFP welcomes French Ambassador","slug":"csafp-welcomes-french-ambassador","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, welcomed the French Ambassador to the Philippines, Her Excellency Marie Fontanel, during her courtesy visit on November 7 to the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In their meeting, the two affirmed the longstanding partnership between the Philippines and France and their common obligation to uphold and enforce international law.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/FA1.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, welcomes Her Excellency Marie Fontanel, French Ambassador to the Philippines, during her visit to the AFP General Headquarters in Quezon City on November 7.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-07T14:26:44+08:00","hits":277},{"id":657,"title":"PASSING THE TORCH | OACPA","slug":"passing-the-torch-oacpa","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Chief, Public Affairs Office, Col. Xerxes A Trinidad formally turned over his duties as Army Chief, Public Affairs to Lt.Col. Louie Dema-ala during a Change of Chiefs of Office Ceremony presided by MGen Potenciano C Camba, Chief of Staff, Philippine Army on November 7, 2023 at the Headquarters, Philippine Army, Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City.</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/OAC1.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Potenciano Camba, Chief of Staff, Philippine Army presents the Command Plaque to Col. Xerxes Trinidad PA during the Change of Chief of Office Ceremony of the Office of the Army Chief Public Affairs on November 7, 2023 in Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-07T07:47:15+08:00","hits":875},{"id":658,"title":"CELEBRATING TRADITIONS | ","slug":"celebrating-traditions","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines formally opened the AFP's entry for  the \"16th Belenismo sa Tarlac\" with the Secretary of National Defense, Gilberto  Teodoro Jr as the Guest of Honor and Keynote Speaker in San Miguel, Tarlac City on November 6, 2023.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">\"Belenismo sa Tarlac\" is a competition and advocacy conducted annually in the country's Belen capital. It showcases festive displays of Belens from different communities in Tarlac and features various recreation of the nativity scene. </p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/BEL2.jpg","image_caption":"Defense Secretary Gilberto Teodoro Jr and the Chief of Staff, AFP, General Romeo Brawner Jr with army troops during the Opening of the AFP Belen for the 16th Belenismo sa Tarlac on November 6, 2023.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-07T06:10:25+08:00","hits":316},{"id":659,"title":"AFP Chief attends Basa Runway Dedication Ceremony","slug":"afp-chief-attends-basa-runway-dedication-ceremony","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA attended the Basa Air Base Enhanced Defense Cooperation Agreement (EDCA) Runway Dedication Ceremony on November 6, 2023 in Floridablanca, Pampanga. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Defense Secretary Gilberto C Teodoro Jr, and US Deputy Chief of Mission to the Philippines, Mr. Robert Y Ewing headed the ceremony, which marked the completion of the runway's rehabilitation. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/EDCAB1.jpg","image_caption":"Defense Secretary Gilberto Teodoro Jr,  and US Chief of Mission to the Philippines, Mr. Robert Ewing headed the ribbon cutting during the Basa Runway Dedication Ceremony on November 6, 2023 in Floridablanca, Pampanga.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-07T06:09:17+08:00","hits":591},{"id":660,"title":"AFP opens 2023 DAGITPA Exercises","slug":"afp-opens-2023-dagitpa-exercises","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines Joint Exercises Dagat-Langit-Lupa (AJEX DAGITPA) officially opened today, November 6, in a ceremony presided by General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff AFP, at the General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">AJEX DAGITPA will involve more than 1500 active and reserve forces from the Army, Air Force, Navy, Marines, Special Operations Command and Cyber Group in staff, command post, cyber defense, and field training events in the Northern Luzon Command area of responsibility that will last until November 17. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/AJEX2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, poses for a photo with senior military officers during the opening ceremony of AJEX DAGITPA on November 6 at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-06T05:03:23+08:00","hits":1005},{"id":661,"title":"AFP Statement on Japan’s Official Security Assistance (OSA) grant","slug":"afp-statement-on-japan-s-official-security-assistance-osa-grant","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/OSA.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-04T06:20:35+08:00","hits":291},{"id":662,"title":"New Leaders Take the Helm at AFP's Western Mindanao Command and Office of The Inspector General","slug":"new-leaders-take-the-helm-at-afps-western-mindanao-command-and-office-of-the-inspector-general","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) held a joint change of command and chief of office ceremony for Western Mindanao Command (WESMINCOM) and Office of The Inspector General on Friday, 03 November 2023 at the WESMINCOM Gymnasium, Camp Navarro, Upper Calarian, Zamboanga City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Lieutenant General William N. Gonzales, who previously held the position of The Inspector General, AFP, officially assumed as Commander of WESMINCOM. Prior to his previous position, he headed the Joint Task Force Sulu and 11th Infantry Division in concurrent capacity. He is a member of the Philippine Military Academy (PMA) “Makatao” Class of 1989. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/COCWC.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo S Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff, AFP (center) officiates the assumption of Lieutenant General William N Gonzales (left) as the new Commander of Western Mindanao Command and Major General Steve D Crespillo (right) as the new Inspector General, AFP during the joint Change of Command and Chief of Office Ceremony at Camp Navarro, Zamboanga City on Friday, November 3, 2023.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-03T06:14:30+08:00","hits":2167},{"id":663,"title":"Filipinos pay respects to Heroes at Libingan Ng Mga Bayani","slug":"filipinos-pay-respects-to-heroes-at-libingan-ng-mga-bayani","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – A total of 84,300 citizens, including families and loved ones of the departed, have visited the Libingan Ng Mga Bayani (LNMB) from October 31 to November 2, 2023, to give tribute to the heroes of the country during the national observance of Undas. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On November 1 alone, a total of 42,790 visitors flocked LNMB during the observance of All Saints’ Day. The national cemetery serves as the resting place for soldiers, Philippine presidents, national heroes, patriots, artists and scientists. Currently, there are a total of 53, 548 interred in LNMB.   </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/Und2%201.jpg","image_caption":"Two members of the Fort Bonifacio National High School Girl Scout of the Philippines light a candle to one of the tombs at the Libingan Ng Mga Bayani commemorating the legacy of our heroes in preserving peace and freedom in the country as it observes Undas 2023. (Photo by Pvt Angelica Rose M Valderrama (Inf) PA/Office of the Army Chief, Public Affairs)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-02T10:29:33+08:00","hits":535},{"id":664,"title":"On the successful conduct of the Barangay and Sangguniang Kabataan Elections.","slug":"on-the-successful-conduct-of-the-barangay-and-sangguniang-kabataan-elections","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    ","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/NOVEMBER%202023/bske2%201.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-11-01T10:26:31+08:00","hits":411},{"id":665,"title":"CSAFP's Message on the observance of the All Saints Day and All Souls Day","slug":"csafps-message-on-the-observance-of-the-all-saints-day-and-all-souls-day","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I am one with the nation in the observance of All Saints Day and All Souls Day.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This season is an invitation for us to honor all the saints, both known and unknown, and celebrate the lives of our departed loved ones. We also take the time to honor the legacy, memory, and patriotic deeds of our fallen comrades who selflessly dedicated their lives in service to the country and made the ultimate sacrifice.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/und%201.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-31T10:15:56+08:00","hits":406},{"id":666,"title":"CSAFP Statement on the BSKE 2023","slug":"csafp-statement-on-the-bske-2023","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">I enjoin my fellow Filipinos to exercise their right to vote and select the next leaders of their communities this coming Barangay and Sangguniang Kabataan Elections on October 30. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Let's not take this right for granted. Instead, let's take this as an opportunity to further improve our government, starting from its most basic unit, our barangays and our youth leaders.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/bske1%201.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-30T10:12:42+08:00","hits":407},{"id":667,"title":"ROTC wins in latest national cadets games","slug":"rotc-wins-in-latest-national-cadets-games","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--Senator Francis Tolentino lauded the just concluded national championships of the Reserve Officers Training Course (ROTC) Games for fulfilling its goal to raise awareness on and rally support for the military training program for the youth.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The ROTC Games held its closing ceremony on October 28 at the Philippine Air Force Gymnasium in Pasay City and awarded the cadets who scored a podium finish in different professionally sanctioned events.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/rotcg%201.jpg","image_caption":"Cadet-athletes who competed in the 2023 ROTC Games attend its closing ceremony on October 28 in Pasay City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-29T10:00:40+08:00","hits":285},{"id":668,"title":"Army cadets crowned champions in 2023 ROTC Games","slug":"army-cadets-crowned-champions-in-2023-rotc-games","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--Philippine Army cadets were hailed as the overall champion of the Philippine Reserve Officers Training Course (ROTC) Games that concluded on October 28 at the Philippine Air Force Gymnasium in Pasay City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">They bagged a total of 54 medals, with 20 golds, 16 silvers, and 18 bronze in the national championship games that capped the two-month competition across the Philippines.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/arotc%201.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Potenciano Camba PA, the Chief of Staff, Philippine Army receives the trophy for the Philippine Army as the overall champion of the Philippine ROTC Games on October 28 in Pasay City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-29T08:05:34+08:00","hits":543},{"id":669,"title":"AFP, Canada conclude business planning course","slug":"afp-canada-conclude-business-planning-course","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the Directorate of Military Training Cooperation of the Canadian Armed Forces concluded the Business Planning Course 2023, a training activity they co-hosted, in Clark, Pampanga from October 23-27. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">BPC aimed to enhance strategic planning, resource management, and decision-making skills. Thirty-three military and civilian students from eight different countries participated in the activity.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/bpc%201.jpg","image_caption":"Participants of the Business Planning Course pose for a photo with Major Neville Rabadi Ret (5th from left, front row), one of the instructors in the week-long training activity held on October 23-27 in Clark, Pampanga.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-28T09:50:17+08:00","hits":226},{"id":670,"title":"31 AFP officers take oath in Malacañang","slug":"31-afp-officers-take-oath-in-malacanang","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Thirty-one newly promoted generals and flag officers led by the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo Brawner Jr, took their oath of office before the President and Commander in Chief, His Excellency Ferdinand Marcos Jr, on October 27 in Malacañan Palace.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The oath-taking signifies the officers’ commitment to the performance of their duties and responsibilities as public servants and leaders who will steer the AFP in the accomplishment of its mandate of protecting the people and securing the state.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/oath.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr presides over the oath-taking ceremony of the 31 newly promoted generals and flag officers of the Armed Forces of the Philippines with the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo Brawner Jr, on stage on October 27 in Malacañan Palace.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-28T09:41:20+08:00","hits":403},{"id":671,"title":"AFP installs new public affairs chief","slug":"afp-installs-new-public-affairs-chief","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) formally installed Col Xerxes Trinidad as the new chief of the Public Affairs Office AFP (PAOAFP) on October 27 at the General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Col Trinidad replaced LtCol Enrico Gil Ileto, who moved on to pursue full time his Master’s in National Security Administration, in the ceremony presided by LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/PAO1.jpg","image_caption":"Col Xerxes Trinidad (right) and LtCol Enrico Gil Ileto (left), the new and former chief of the PAOAFP respectively, and presiding officer LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan (middle) during the Change of Chief of Office of PAOAFP on October 27 at the AFP General Headquarters.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-27T07:42:09+08:00","hits":1863},{"id":672,"title":"Former PSG commander assumes command of CRSAFP","slug":"former-psg-commander-assumes-command-of-crsafp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) formally installed BGen Ramon Zagala as the commander of the Civil Relations Service AFP (CRSAFP) in a change of command ceremony on October 26 here. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">He replaced BGen Arvin Lagamon who assumed as the new Deputy Chief of Staff for Civil-Military Operations, J7, on October 24.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/CRSPSG1.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Arthur Cordura, VCSAFP, gives the CRSAFP flag to its new commander, BGen Ramon Zagala, during the Change of Command Ceremony of CRSAFP on October 26 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. (Photo by CRSAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-26T08:59:20+08:00","hits":2717},{"id":673,"title":"CSAFP welcomes APCSS director","slug":"csafp-welcomes-apcss-director","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, welcomed Rear Admiral Peter Gumataotao (Ret), Director of the Daniel K. Inouye Asia-Pacific Center for Security Studies (APCSS) during the latter’s courtesy visit on October 26 at the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In their meeting, the two discussed training and education opportunities in the APCSS and exchanged perspectives on present and emerging security issues and threats and how to address them.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/AFPCSS2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, CSAFP, and Rear Admiral Peter Gumataotao (Ret), Director of the Daniel K. Inouye Asia-Pacific Center for Security Studies (APCSS), during the latter’s courtesy visit on October 26 at the AFP General Headquarters, Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-26T08:56:27+08:00","hits":666},{"id":674,"title":"AFP, AFPSLAI break ground for Modular Transient Facility","slug":"afp-afpslai-break-ground-for-modular-transient-facility","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines and VAdm Gaudencio Collado Jr (Ret), Chief Executive Officer and President of the Armed Forces and Police Savings and Loans Association, Inc. (AFPSLAI), led the groundbreaking ceremony and signing of the memorandum of agreement for the modular transient facility project on October 25 here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The project, consisting of one cluster of living spaces, is part of AFPSLAI’s corporate social responsibility program and seeks to provide quality temporary accommodation to AFP personnel visiting Camp Aguinaldo. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/MGC1.jpg","image_caption":"CSAFP General Romeo Brawner Jr, AFPSLAI President and CEO VAdm Gaudencio Collado Jr, AFP Chief Engineer MGen Proceso Rebancos, and contractor Ms Susan Oris break ground on the site of the Camp Aguinaldo modular transient facility project on October 25. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-25T03:28:11+08:00","hits":1096},{"id":675,"title":"AFP installs new chiefs to CMO, strategy offices","slug":"afp-installs-new-chiefs-to-cmo-strategy-offices","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines installed new officers to lead the Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff for Civil-Military Office, OJ7, and the Office for Strategic Studies and Strategy Management (OSSSM) in a ceremony at the AFP General Headquarters on October 24.</p>\r\n<p>BGen Arvin Lagamon formally assumed as the new J7 following his stint as the Commander of the Civil Relations Service AFP. He replaced MGen Gabriel Viray III.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/CMO3.jpg","image_caption":"The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP, Marine LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, delivers his remarks during the Joint Change of Chief of Office Ceremony for the Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff for CMO, OJ7, and the Office for Strategic Studies and Strategy Management on October 24 at the AFP General Headquarters (Photo by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-24T11:20:37+08:00","hits":2652},{"id":676,"title":"AFP joins send-off of election-duty forces","slug":"afp-joins-send-off-of-election-duty-forces","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/ELE3.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/ELE3.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>COMELEC, PNP, AFP, PCG, and DepEd officials led by Chairman George Erwin Garcia pose for a photo with the multi-agency force that will secure the BSKE 2023 during a send-off and turnover ceremony in Camp Crame on October 27. (Photo by John Boboyo/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), represented by The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, joined the turnover and send-off ceremony of the mutli-agency force that will help ensure security, order, and integrity of the 2023 Barangay and Sangguniang Kabataan Elections (BSKE) on October 30.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">More than 1,100 personnel from the AFP, Philippine National Police, Philippine Coast Guard, and Department of Education were present in the ceremony held at the PNP headquarters in Camp Crame on October 23 and attended by Commission on Elections Chairman George Erwin Garcia.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/ELE3.jpg","image_caption":"COMELEC, PNP, AFP, PCG, and DepEd officials led by Chairman George Erwin Garcia pose for a photo with the multi-agency force that will secure the BSKE 2023 during a send-off and turnover ceremony in Camp Crame on October 27. (Photo by John Boboyo/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-24T00:28:29+08:00","hits":706},{"id":677,"title":"Render unwavering allegiance to nation, Brawner tells AFP","slug":"render-unwavering-allegiance-to-nation-brawner-tells-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/OOC1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/OOC1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>Col Rosel Tan, Deputy Chief of the Offices of Ethical Standards and Public Accountability, leads the Renewal of Pledge of Allegiance to the AFP Code of Conduct during the commemoration of the 33rd anniversary of the AFP Code of Conduct on October 23 at the AFP General Headquarters. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, called on officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian employees of the military to be reminded of their duty to the flag and maintain unwavering allegiance to the country at the General Headquarters here on October 23.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP is commemorating the 33rd anniversary of its Code of Conduct highlighted by the renewal of pledge of allegiance to the AFP Code of Conduct. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/OOC1.jpg","image_caption":"Col Rosel Tan, Deputy Chief of the Offices of Ethical Standards and Public Accountability, leads the Renewal of Pledge of Allegiance to the AFP Code of Conduct during the commemoration of the 33rd anniversary of the AFP Code of Conduct on October 23 at the AFP General Headquarters. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-23T02:09:13+08:00","hits":966},{"id":678,"title":"CSAFP, EU Ambassador welcome more engagements","slug":"csafp-eu-ambassador-welcome-more-engagements","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/bri1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"638\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/bri1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>General Romeo Brawner Jr receives EU Ambassador Luc Véron during the latter’s visit to the AFP General Headquarters on October 20. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), and H.E. Luc Véron, Ambassador of the European Union (EU) to the Philippines, are expecting more engagements between the Philippines and EU member states in the future.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The two met and discussed pertinent security matters during the ambassador’s courtesy visit at the AFP General Headquarters here on October 20.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/bri1.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr receives EU Ambassador Luc Véron during the latter’s visit to the AFP General Headquarters on October 20. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-21T10:06:49+08:00","hits":441},{"id":679,"title":"AFP Chief expresses soaring confidence in Sergeants Major","slug":"afp-chief-expresses-soaring-confidence-in-sergeants-major","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/SM5.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/SM5.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>AFP Chief, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA poses for a photo with AFP Senior Enlisted Personnel during the Closing Ceremony of the Annual Year-End Consultative Meeting CY 2023 on October 20 in Camp Aguinaldo. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA, The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP) expressed his confidence in the AFP’s Sergeants Major during the Closing Ceremony of the Senior Enlisted Leaders Year-End Consultative Meeting 2023 on October 20.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Also celebrating the 27th Non-Commissioned Officers Week and the 54th Founding Anniversary of the Office of the AFP Sergeant Major, the CSAFP also shared his objective of elevating the level of confidence and competence of Senior Enlisted Personnel.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/SM5.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA poses for a photo with AFP Senior Enlisted Personnel during the Closing Ceremony of the Annual Year-End Consultative Meeting CY 2023 on October 20 in Camp Aguinaldo. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-20T06:02:13+08:00","hits":823},{"id":680,"title":"VALOR AND VICTORY ","slug":"valor-and-victory","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </p>\r\n<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/viber_image_2023-10-20_09-32-08-807.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"638\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/viber_image_2023-10-20_09-32-08-807.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>Sgt Jason D Huerte PAF and A1C Rheyjey C Ortouste PAF. soldier-athletes of the Sepaktakraw event in which they won bronze medals in the Men's Regu and Men's Quadrant categories in the recently concluded 19 Asian Games held at Hangzhou, China.</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Congratulations to our inspiring soldier-athletes who represented our country and the AFP in the recently-held Asian Games 2023 and 1st UNTV Volleyball League.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Sgt Jason D Huerte PAF and A1C Rheyjey C Ortouste PAF bagged bronze medals in the Men’s Regu and Men’s Quadrant categories as part of the Sepaktakraw National Team that competed in Hangzhou, China.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Meanwhile, the AFP Lady Gunnar secured the Championship in the inaugural UNTV Volleyball League last October 15, 2023. The team won an amount of PhP500,00.00 which will be given to the AFP Educational Benefit System Office as their chosen beneficiary.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">📷: Special Service, AFP</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/AS.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Lady Gunnar takes the GOLD in the UNTV Volleyball League Season 1. FIVE HUNDRED THOUSAND PESOS (PhP500,000.00) worth of prize money will be given to the AFP Educational Benefit System Office (AFP EBSO) as their chosen beneficiary.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-20T02:43:02+08:00","hits":476},{"id":681,"title":"AFP Chief to Naval Air Wing: Surpass your limits","slug":"afp-chief-to-naval-air-wing-surpass-your-limits","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/Sang5.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"551\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/Sang5.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>The Chief of Staff, AFP, Gen. Romeo S Brawner Jr, with the Naval Aviators from the Naval Air Wing during their 76th Founding Anniversary on October 18. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City –The Naval Air Wing of the Philippine Navy was challenged by the AFP Chief to go beyond what is asked of the unit during its anniversary celebration, October 18 in Sangley Point, Cavite City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“May we forever prioritize safety as a cornerstone of our operational success. Together, we will uphold the core values of the Naval Air Wing – soaring safely towards unparalleled excellence. I would like to challenge you to try to surpass the limits that you have set for your unit. Mahirap ang trabaho ng isang aviator, especially when you will be flying for missions to ensure the territorial integrity of our country,” Gen Romeo Brawner Jr., Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff (CSAFP) said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/Sang5.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, AFP, Gen. Romeo S Brawner Jr, with the Naval Aviators from the Naval Air Wing during their 76th Founding Anniversary on October 18. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-19T01:13:52+08:00","hits":814},{"id":682,"title":"AFP officers take new posts","slug":"afp-officers-take-new-posts","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Several high-ranking officers of the Armed Forces of the Philippines are expected to assume new positions following an order of appointments approved by President Ferdinand Marcos Jr.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">LtGen William Gonzales, the Inspector General AFP, was designated as the new Commander of Western Mindanao Command. He will swap places with MGen Steve Crespillo.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-18T02:41:44+08:00","hits":1364},{"id":683,"title":"General Brawner returns to, celebrates Marawi City","slug":"general-brawner-returns-to-celebrates-marawi-city","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/mar1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/mar1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>OPAPRU Secretary Carlito Galvez Jr and CSAFP General Romeo Brawner Jr render a salute to the monument commemorating the fallen government troops in the Marawi City campaign at the 103rd Brigade headquarters on October 17 in Marawi City. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo Brawner Jr, returned on October 17 to Marawi to celebrate the city’s liberation from IS-linked terrorists.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Fresh from his studies in the US Army War College, General Brawner, who called Marawi City his second home, recalled during his speech in the commemoration ceremony how he volunteered to participate in the campaign to free the city in 2017.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/mar1.jpg","image_caption":"OPAPRU Secretary Carlito Galvez Jr and CSAFP General Romeo Brawner Jr render a salute to the monument commemorating the fallen government troops in the Marawi City campaign at the 103rd Brigade headquarters on October 17 in Marawi City. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-17T05:12:17+08:00","hits":799},{"id":684,"title":"CSAFP, UK ambassador tackle West PH Sea issues in meet","slug":"csafp-uk-ambassador-tackle-west-ph-sea-issues-in-meet","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/UK2 1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"637\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/UK2 1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>General Romeo Brawner Jr, the CSAFP, receives UK Ambassador Laure Beaufils to the AFP General Headquarters during her visit on October 16. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, and HMA Laure Beaufils, UK’s Ambassador to the Philippines, talked of enhancing PH-UK defense partnership amid pressing issues in the West Philippine Sea.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">HMA Beaufils visited the AFP General Headquarters here on October 16 and was welcomed by the CSAFP along with members of the Joint Staff and the AFP Surgeon General.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/UK2%201.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, the CSAFP, receives UK Ambassador Laure Beaufils to the AFP General Headquarters during her visit on October 16. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-16T08:38:11+08:00","hits":642},{"id":685,"title":"PH, Vietnam boost partnership for operational value in Southeast Asia","slug":"ph-vietnam-boost-partnership-for-operational-value-in-southeast-asia","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/VIE4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"532\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/VIE4.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>The delegates of the 8th Philippines-Vietnam Senior Officer’s Exchange Visit Program (SOEVP) pose for a photo with the AFP’s Senior Officers during their Courtesy Call on October 16 at the General Headquarters. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Vice Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, LtGen Arthur Cordura PAF expressed his confidence in sharing a “growing and progressive operational value” in Southeast Asia as he welcomed the delegates of the 8th Philippines-Vietnam Senior Officer’s Exchange Visit Program (SOEVP), headed by Sr. Col. Le Van Phan, Deputy Commander, Military Corp 1, Viet Nam People’s Army (VPA) in a Courtesy Call on October 16 at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“Our Armed Forces and yours have been sharing a growing and progressive operational value in Southeast Asia. For the longest time, we have endeavored to enhance our partnership. We hope that your delegation will enjoy the interactions here with our senior officers and be able to immerse yourselves in the culture that we have. We are optimistic that this visit will be productive for both our Armed Forces,” expressed LtGen Cordura.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/VIE4.jpg","image_caption":"The delegates of the 8th Philippines-Vietnam Senior Officer’s Exchange Visit Program (SOEVP) pose for a photo with the AFP’s Senior Officers during their Courtesy Call on October 16 at the General Headquarters. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-16T08:07:20+08:00","hits":766},{"id":686,"title":"Philippine Navy vessel warns off China’s Navy vessel for dangerous maneuvers inside Pag-Asa Territorial Sea","slug":"philippine-navy-vessel-warns-off-china-s-navy-vessel-for-dangerous-maneuvers-inside-pag-asa-territorial-sea","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/WARN.jpg\" width=\"828\" height=\"458\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/WARN.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Philippine Navy’s (PN) BRP Benguet (LS507) warned off and issued consecutive radio challenges to China’s People’s Liberation Army Navy Ship 621 (PLAN 621) after it shadowed the former at an 80-yard distance and attempted to cross LS507's bow with a CPA (closest point of approach) of 350 yards at 5.8 Nautical Miles South West of Pag-asa Island on Friday, October 13. The PN vessel was en-route to Rizal Reef Station for the conduct of a regular rotation and resupply (RoRe) mission when the incident happened.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The PN crew cited the violation of the Collision Regulations (COLREG) in its radio challenges, and demanded that the Chinese vessel to steer clear of the BRP Benguet.  </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/WARN.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-15T10:53:54+08:00","hits":1429},{"id":687,"title":"AFP Mental Health Program","slug":"afp-mental-health-program","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/215f3aef-9d7b-4db5-becd-2ce1442ea00f.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/215f3aef-9d7b-4db5-becd-2ce1442ea00f.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>The Office of the Surgeon General leads the launching of the AFP Mental Health Program on October 12, 2023 with The Deputy Chief of Staff Lieutenant General Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M) in attendance. (Photo by PO3 Viluan PN (Ret), PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In the wake of World Mental Health Day, the Armed Forces of the Philippines through the Office of the Surgeon General launched its Mental Health Program on October 12, 2023 with The Deputy Chief of Staff Lieutenant General Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M) representing the AFP Chief of Staff as the Guest of Honor and Speaker.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The event was highlighted by the introduction of the AFP Mental Health Web Pages to improve access to mental health support, ensuring the ongoing efforts to address challenges that may impact personnel well-being and organizational performance. The event also honored benevolent stakeholders for their contributions to the cause.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/215f3aef-9d7b-4db5-becd-2ce1442ea00f.jpg","image_caption":"The Office of the Surgeon General leads the launching of the AFP Mental Health Program on October 12, 2023 with The Deputy Chief of Staff Lieutenant General Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M) in attendance. (Photo by PO3 Viluan PN (Ret), PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-13T05:02:37+08:00","hits":2822},{"id":688,"title":"AFP, UK affirm commitment to defense relations","slug":"afp-uk-affirm-commitment-to-defense-relations","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/UK2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"582\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/UK2.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>MGen Gabriel Viray III leads the foyer honors for Baroness Annabel Goldie during her visit to the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo on October 12. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines represented by LtGen William Gonzales, the AFP Inspector General, and Baroness Annabel Goldie, the UK’s Minister of State for Indo-Pacific Defence Engagement, reaffirmed PH-UK's commitment to strengthen defense relations during her visit at the AFP General Headquarters on October 12.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In their meeting, the two discussed increasing PH-UK military engagements supported by the 2017 Memorandum of Understanding on Defense Cooperation that is rooted in a long history of friendship and defence cooperation engagements.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/UK2.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Gabriel Viray III leads the foyer honors for Baroness Annabel Goldie during her visit to the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo on October 12. (Photo by Sgt Ambay/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-13T00:28:10+08:00","hits":865},{"id":689,"title":"Brawner to Security Sector Athletes: Filipinos depend on us for Peace and Freedom","slug":"brawner-to-security-sector-athletes-filipinos-depend-on-us-for-peace-and-freedom","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image align-center\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/OLY1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/OLY1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>Participants from the Philippine Army during the Opening Ceremony of the Olympics 2023 on October 10 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Officially marking the beginning of friendly competitions among Philippine uniformed services, atheletes participating in the AFP-PNP-PCG-BFP-BJMP Olympics 2023 were reminded of their role for peace and freedom of Filipinos in an opening ceremony October 10 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand here. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“This event is one way for us to develop our camaraderie. Being members of the uniformed services of the Philippines, we are a proud organization. Marami po sa ating mga kababayan ang umaasa sa atin para sa kalayaan ng ating bayan at sa kapayaaan,” said the Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA, the Guest of Honor and Speaker. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/OLY1.jpg","image_caption":"Participants from the Philippine Army during the Opening Ceremony of the Olympics 2023 on October 10 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-11T05:38:49+08:00","hits":647},{"id":690,"title":"CSAFP, Korean Ambassador to PH, discuss mutual support","slug":"csafp-korean-ambassador-to-ph-discuss-mutual-support","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/THA.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/THA.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>AFP Chief of Staff, General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA welcomes Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Republic of Korea (ROK) to the Philippines, His Excellency Lee Sang-Hwa, during his visit to the General Headquarters on October 10. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP) General Romeo S Brawner Jr, welcomed the Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Republic of Korea (ROK) to the Philippines, His Excellency Lee Sang-Hwa in an Introductory Courtesy Call on October 10 at the AFP Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“We are indeed very honored that you came to visit us. It goes to show the importance and value that you give to the Armed Forces of the Philippines and the relationship of our Armed Forces,” said the CSAFP as he conveyed his gratitude to the envoy. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/THA.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff, General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA welcomes Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Republic of Korea (ROK) to the Philippines, His Excellency Lee Sang-Hwa, during his visit to the General Headquarters on October 10. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-10T08:18:52+08:00","hits":692},{"id":691,"title":"CSAFP visit to Pag-asa Island","slug":"csafp-visit-to-pag-asa-island","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Romeo Brawner Jr, the AFP Chief of Staff, and VAdm Alberto Carlos, Commander of the Western Command, accompany the Speaker of the House of Representatives HE Ferdinand Martin Romualdez who visited the Pag-asa Island in Kalayaan, Palawan on October 5. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The party, composed of  Majority Leader Manuel Jose \"Mannix\" Dalipe, Minority Leader Marcelino Libanan, and Committee on Appropriation Chairman and Ako Bicol Party List Representative Zaldy Co, inspected ongoing government projects in the island.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In a statement, the CSAFP said he was happy with the progress of projects in the island. \"The last time I was there, the runway, the surface of the runway was still dirt.  But this time when we landed,  we landed on concrete. It was very nice.  It was extended.  And I also saw that there was electricity already in the area.  The last time I was there,  there was no electricity,\" General Brawner claimed.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">He also thanked the Speaker for proposing to allocate at least Php3-billion for development projects on Pag-asa Island, which will include airport reclamation extension, the naval port, and fishing sanctuary./// (Photo and quote by House of Representatives)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/PR%20PHOTOS%202023/October/386163370_717581510404549_6145078561118208754_n.jpg","image_caption":"The party of House Speaker Ferdinand Martin Romualdez pose for a commemorative photo on Pag-asa Island during their visit on October 5.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-06T04:57:43+08:00","hits":953},{"id":692,"title":"AFP meets outgoing and incoming Thai defense attachés to PH","slug":"afp-meets-outgoing-and-incoming-thai-defense-attaches-to-ph","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/THA1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/OCTOBER 2023/THA1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>Group Capt Nirut Rattanajanya, incoming Thai Defense Attaché to the Philippines, presents a memento to LtGen William Gonzales PA, The Inspector General, AFP, and the Acting The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, in a Joint Introductory and Exit Call conducted on October 03 at the General Headquarters. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – LtGen William Gonzales PA, The Inspector General, AFP, and the Acting The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, welcomed the incoming and outgoing Defense Attachés of Thailand to the Philippines in a Joint Introductory and Exit Call conducted on October 03 at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“We would like to thank you for your services here for the last three years, and I hope you gained a lot of experience. We are very thankful for your time and assistance to the Armed Forces of the Philippines,” said LtGen Gonzales to the outgoing Thai Attaché, Group Capt Soonthorn Pongampai.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/OCTOBER%202023/THA1.jpg","image_caption":"Group Capt Nirut Rattanajanya, incoming Thai Defense Attaché to the Philippines, presents a memento to LtGen William Gonzales PA, The Inspector General, AFP, and the Acting The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, in a Joint Introductory and Exit Call conducted on October 03 at the General Headquarters. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-03T06:04:02+08:00","hits":923},{"id":693,"title":"AFP wraps up 2023 National Reservist Week Celebration","slug":"afp-wraps-up-2023-national-reservist-week-celebration","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/res1 1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/res1 1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>The 27th Naval Affiliated Reserve Group performs a capability demonstration during the 2023 National Reservist Week Culmination Program on September 30 in Camp Aguinaldo. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines, through the Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff for Reservist and Retiree Affairs, J9, officially marked the end of the month-long celebration of the 44th National Reservist Week in a culmination program on September 30.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Defense Secretary Gilberto Teodoro Jr. served as the Guest of Honor and Speaker during the culmination ceremony. “We are in the process of redesigning our reserve force based on the needs of the times. Hopefully, we can come up with a synergistic, ready, and relevant Reserve Force not only now but lay the foundations for building it and changing the shape as needed in the future,” Sec. Teodoro Jr. said.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/res1%201.jpg","image_caption":"The 27th Naval Affiliated Reserve Group performs a capability demonstration during the 2023 National Reservist Week Culmination Program on September 30 in Camp Aguinaldo. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-10-01T02:12:22+08:00","hits":1832},{"id":694,"title":"Peace as every citizen’s responsibility: AFP holds Peace Symposium 2023","slug":"peace-as-every-citizen-s-responsibility-afp-holds-peace-symposium-2023","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/PS2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/PS2.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>The speakers with the Chief, AFPPDO, Capt Norsal Dimaporo PN and The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M) during the Peace Symposium 2023 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. (Photo by PO3 Viluan PN (Ret) /PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – In commemoration of the 2023 National Peace Consciousness Month, a Peace Symposium was facilitated by the Armed Forces of the Philippines Peace and Development Office (AFPPDO) on September 28.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“We gather here to explore the intricate nature of peacebuilding in a rapidly changing world. Let us embrace this opportunity to further enhance our knowledge, strengthen our partnerships, and reaffirm our commitment to a more peaceful and secure world. The gains of peace are often very fragile, and consolidating these gains remains to be our key responsibility,” said the Guest of Honor and Speaker, Office of the Special Assistant to the President, Secretary Antonio Ernesto Lagdameo Jr., in a message delivered by Asst. Secretary Ria Danielle Lumapas.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/PS2.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-29T00:39:54+08:00","hits":1225},{"id":695,"title":"Philippine Navy hosts Exercise SAMASAMA","slug":"philippine-navy-hosts-exercise-samasama","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"850\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Philippine Navy is set to host this year’s iteration of the PH-US Exercise SAMASAMA that is scheduled from 02 to 13 October 2023 at the Naval Forces Southern Luzon (NFSL) Area of Operations. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">SAMASAMA is a bilateral exercise between the United States Navy (USN) and the Philippine Navy (PN) that aims to further strengthen international defense cooperation and advance a rules-based international order.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-27T00:08:50+08:00","hits":2438},{"id":696,"title":"AFP Chief to PH Navy: fight for our sovereign rights and territorial integrity","slug":"afp-chief-to-ph-navy-fight-for-our-sovereign-rights-and-territorial-integrity","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/PN2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/PN2.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>The Chief of Staff, AFP, General Romeo S Brawner PA greets the Philippine Navy troops during his Official Visit to their Headquarters on September 26. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Navy personnel were reminded by the Armed Forces Chief today to fight for the nation’s sovereign rights and territory during his visit at the Navy Headquarters this morning. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“Let us always bear in mind our own interests. We are Filipinos, and we will fight for the Philippines’ rights, our sovereign rights, and our territorial integrity,” General Romeo S Brawner Jr, the Armed Forces of the Philippines Chief of Staff said. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/PN2.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, AFP, General Romeo S Brawner PA greets the Philippine Navy troops during his Official Visit to their Headquarters on September 26. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-26T08:50:18+08:00","hits":1083},{"id":697,"title":"CSAFP lauds PAF’s support to ground troops, ops","slug":"csafp-lauds-paf-s-support-to-ground-troops-ops","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/PAF4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/PAF4.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>General Romeo Brawner Jr, the CSAFP, poses for a photo with the officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian employees of the Philippine Air Force at the Villamor Air Base during his official visit and talk to troops on September 25. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, lauded the Philippine Air Force for its dedication towards serving the country as he thanked its pilots and crew who have supported ground troops in its operations over the years.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CSAFP gave this message to the officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian employees in Villamor Air Base during his visit and talk to troops on September 25.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/PAF4.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, the CSAFP, poses for a photo with the officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian employees of the Philippine Air Force at the Villamor Air Base during his official visit and talk to troops on September 25. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-25T06:26:57+08:00","hits":848},{"id":698,"title":"Tourists flock to 6ID’s ‘Symbol of Peace’","slug":"tourists-flock-to-6id-s-symbol-of-peace","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/pea.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"567\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/pea.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>MGen Alex Rillera, 6ID Commander, poses for a photo with visitors of the Symbol of Peace in Camp Siongco, Datu Odin Sinsuat, Maguindanao Del Norte.</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Symbol of Peace inaugurated on Thursday, September 21, is now attracting tourists and raising awareness on the government’s whole-of-nation efforts to end all armed conflict.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The monument is an eighteen-foot replica of an M-16 crafted from dismantled firearms that were confiscated, captured, recovered or were surrendered to the military as part of its efforts to end violence and proliferation of illegal firearms in the Bangsamoro region.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/pea.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Alex Rillera, 6ID Commander, poses for a photo with visitors of the Symbol of Peace in Camp Siongco, Datu Odin Sinsuat, Maguindanao Del Norte.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-22T06:02:48+08:00","hits":855},{"id":699,"title":"PH, Canadian Navy sail together in WPS","slug":"ph-canadian-navy-sail-together-in-wps","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/SAIL1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"638\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/SAIL1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>Philippine Navy's BRP Antonio Luna (FF151) and the Canadian Navy's HMCS Ottawa during their joint sail on September 21 in the West Philippine Sea. (Photo from WESCOM)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--More nations are sailing with the Philippines as the Philippine Navy guided-missile frigate BRP Antonio Luna (FF151) completed a bilateral sail in the West Philippine Sea on September 21 this time with the Canadian Halifax-class frigate HMCS Ottawa (FFH341).</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Starting at around 7:23 in the morning, the two ships met and established radio communications in the vicinity of Malampaya Natural Gas Platform and performed maneuvers for Officers of the Watch (OOWs) that lasted until around 10 o'clock. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/SAIL1.jpg","image_caption":"Philippine Navy's BRP Antonio Luna (FF151) and the Canadian Navy's HMCS Ottawa during their joint sail on September 21 in the West Philippine Sea. (Photo from WESCOM)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-22T05:56:16+08:00","hits":932},{"id":700,"title":"INTERNATIONAL DAY OF PEACE","slug":"international-day-of-peace","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/IDP1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/IDP1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>In celebration of the International Day of Peace, personnel from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined the Peace One Day Forum 2023 initiated by the Rotary International District 3830 on September 21 at the Asia Pacific College, Makati City. (Photo by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Coinciding with the International Day of Peace, the role of the men and women in uniform in peacebuilding was recognized by the Rotary International District 3830 during the Peace One Day Forum 2023 on September 21 at the Asia Pacific College, Makati City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines joined the Rotary-initiated forum which focused on the Quest for a Hopeful and Peaceful World and provided an in-depth understanding of the country's current peace and security landscape. It also serves as a call to action for law enforcement bodies and the community to collectively work together in promoting peace amidst challenges./// (Photo by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAOAFP)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/IDP1.jpg","image_caption":"In celebration of the International Day of Peace, personnel from the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined the Peace One Day Forum 2023 initiated by the Rotary International District 3830 on September 21 at the Asia Pacific College, Makati City. (Photo by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-21T08:14:00+08:00","hits":491},{"id":701,"title":"CSAFP calls for talks to end divide","slug":"csafp-calls-for-talks-to-end-divide","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/DIV2.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/DIV2.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>General Romeo Brawner Jr with OPAPRU Secretary Carlito Garlvez Jr and other guests lead the unveiling of the Symbol of Peace on September 21 at the headquarters of 6th Infantry Division in Maguindanao del Norte. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAO, AFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), called for ‘meaningful conversations’ to end conflict and foster understanding during the unveiling and blessing of the Symbol of Peace on September 21 at the headquarters of 6th Infantry Division in Maguindanao del Norte.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The monument is an eighteen-foot replica of an M-16 crafted from dismantled firearms that were confiscated, captured, recovered or were surrendered to the military as part of its efforts to end violence and proliferation of illegal firearms in the Bangsamoro region.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/DIV2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr with OPAPRU Secretary Carlito Garlvez Jr and other guests lead the unveiling of the Symbol of Peace on September 21 at the headquarters of 6th Infantry Division in Maguindanao del Norte. (Photo by PFC Carmelotes/PAO, AFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-21T04:24:48+08:00","hits":633},{"id":702,"title":"Philippine Navy flagship interacts with Royal Canadian Navy counterparts departing from their recent goodwill visit","slug":"philippine-navy-flagship-interacts-with-royal-canadian-navy-counterparts-departing-from-their-recent-goodwill-visit","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/CAN1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"847\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/CAN1.jpg\" /></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">BRP JOSE RIZAL (FF150), HMCS OTTAWA, NRU ASTERIX, and CESSNA 353 from Naval Air Wing - Philippine Fleet carried out series of drills on September 19, 2023. They practiced various maneuvers, including DIVTACS, Replenishment at Sea (RAS) Approaches, and Photo exercises. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The interaction was highlighted by a  Passing Exercise to bid farewell to the visiting vessels. The Philippine Navy extends this custom to all foreign navies during their goodwill visit as a gesture of courtesy and respect.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Story and Photo by:  BRP Jose Rizal FF150 - PF)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/CAN1.jpg","image_caption":"Philippine Navy flagship interacts with Royal Canadian Navy counterparts departing from their recent goodwill visit on September 18.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-21T02:43:33+08:00","hits":366},{"id":703,"title":"123 would-be trafficking-in-persons rescued in successful support to law enforcement ops in Sulu","slug":"123-would-be-trafficking-in-persons-rescued-in-successful-support-to-law-enforcement-ops-in-sulu","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/ht1.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"1133\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/ht1.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>The Naval Forces Western Mindanao, thru its Naval Task Force 61 together with other law enforcement agencies, successfully rescued would-be trafficking-in-persons in Brgy. Aluh Bunah, Pangutaran, Sulu on September 19, 2023.</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On September 19, 2023, Naval Forces Western Mindanao (NFWM) and other law enforcement organizations successfully rescued 123 people from becoming victims of human trafficking on Tubalubac Island in Pangutaran, Sulu. Additionally, the operation resulted in the recovery of war materials and illegal drugs<br /><br />The rescued trafficking victims were handed over to Ministry of Social Services and Development-BARMM (MSSD-BARMM) for documentation and assistance. The seized evidence was taken to CIDG Sulu-PFU for documentation and proper handling. Reports reveal that most of the rescued victims were from Cebu and Bohol, and they were forced to do difficult labor in spearfishing while being compelled to consume illegal drugs, specifically shabu, to cope with their difficult work conditions.<br /><br />(Story and Photo by: <span class=\"xv78j7m\" spellcheck=\"false\">Naval Forces Western Mindanao</span>)</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/ht1.jpg","image_caption":"The Naval Forces Western Mindanao, thru its Naval Task Force 61 together with other law enforcement agencies, successfully rescued would-be trafficking-in-persons in Brgy. Aluh Bunah, Pangutaran, Sulu on September 19, 2023.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-21T01:10:52+08:00","hits":416},{"id":704,"title":"AFP, Bangladesh mulls defense cooperation through training and education","slug":"afp-bangladesh-mulls-defense-cooperation-through-training-and-education","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/BAN5.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"566\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/BAN5.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>MGen Noel Beleran PN(M), Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8 welcomes BGen Kazi Anisuzzaman, Directing Staff Army-6, National Defense College to the General Headquarters on September 20. (Photos by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — Sharing a similar vision in building good relationships with partner countries, MGen Noel Beleran PN(M), Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8 meets with BGen Kazi Anisuzzaman, Directing Staff Army-6, National Defense College, Mirpur Cantonment in a Courtesy Visit here on September 20.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“We are planning to establish our defense cooperation and our shared responsibility through education and training in pursuit of a more stable Indo-Pacific,” said MGen Beleran.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/BAN5.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Noel Beleran PN(M), Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8 welcomes BGen Kazi Anisuzzaman, Directing Staff Army-6, National Defense College to the General Headquarters on September 20. (Photos by PO3 Viluan Ret/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-21T00:11:41+08:00","hits":480},{"id":705,"title":"AFP, Aus Defence College share practices in training military leaders","slug":"afp-aus-defence-college-share-practices-in-training-military-leaders","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<figure class=\"image\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/ausdc4.jpg\" width=\"850\" height=\"548\" loading=\"lazy\" data-path=\"local-images:/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER 2023/ausdc4.jpg\" />\r\n<figcaption>MGen Noel Beleran PN(M), Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8 hands over a token to Wing Commander Nicholas Pausina, Australian Defence College at the General Headquarters on September 19. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)</figcaption>\r\n</figure>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8, MGen Noel Beleran PN(M) welcomed the delegates of the Australian Command and Staff College headed by the Australian Defence College, Wing Commander Nicholas Pausina in their Study Visit to the country on September 19 at the AFP Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">“We are really looking forward to the opportunity to engage today. It is very much about the opportunity to expand our relationship. We are hoping to learn a lot,” said Wing Commander Pausina.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/SEPTEMBER%202023/ausdc4.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Noel Beleran PN(M), Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8 hands over a token to Wing Commander Nicholas Pausina, Australian Defence College at the General Headquarters on September 19. (Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2023-09-20T00:37:28+08:00","hits":903}]}